    "factsheet": [
        {
            "heading": "Heritage Innovation",
            "paragraphs": [
                "Historic places are not fixed in time—they continue to evolve through careful intervention and creative thinking. This exhibition explores how innovation shapes the way we understand, adapt and extend the life of heritage today—and create the heritage of tomorrow.",
                "Through a curated selection of projects, drawings, material studies and stories, the display reveals how design, research and conservation come together to unlock new possibilities within existing buildings.",
                "A dedicated film screening offers further insight into the processes, people and ideas behind this work—showing how heritage can remain relevant, resilient and alive. Explore the pop-up exhibition at Donald Insall Associates, where you will find a collection of artefacts, records, samples and images that tell the story of places that might be hidden in plain sight."
            ]
        }
    ],
